        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is the difference between CMI Level 5 and Level 7?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              CMI Level 5 is Management and Leadership (units 501 to 526) and Level 7 is Strategic Management and Leadership Practice (units 701 to 716). Each has its own syllabus, unit list and word counts. Level 5 is aimed at practising or aspiring managers who are typically accountable to a senior manager or business owner. Level 7 is aimed at practising or aspiring senior managers and leaders, with roles such as Director and CEO. Level 5 criteria use verbs such as Analyse, Examine and Evaluate, while 37 of the 80 Level 7 criteria begin with Critically. See the CMI Level 5 vs Level 7 guide for a detailed comparison.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Do you help with a specific CMI Level 5 unit?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
